{"name":"Red Peppercorn","hex":"#c62d42","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"},{"term":"peppercorn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The seeds of the pepper plant Piper nigrum, commonly used as a spice, usually ground or crushed.","A small, insignificant quantity; a whit or jot.\n\n A nominal consideration used to satisfy the requirements for the creation of a legal contract."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peppercorn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Black pepper","blocks":[{"text":"Black pepper is a flowering vine in the family Piperaceae, cultivated for its fruit, which is usually dried and used as a spice and seasoning. The fruit is a drupe (stonefruit) which is about 5 mm in diameter, dark red, and contains a stone which encloses a single pepper seed. Peppercorns and the ground pepper derived from them may be described simply as pepper, or more precisely as black pepper, green pepper, or white pepper."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Piper_nigrum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-107.jpg/330px-Piper_nigrum_-_K%C3%B6hler%E2%80%93s_Medizinal-Pflanzen-107.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_pepper"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Black_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg/500px-Black_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Black_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg/1280px-Black_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Black_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg/500px-Black_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Black pepper vine climbing on jackfruit tree (Artocarpus heterophyllus)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlack_Pepper_on_Jackfruit_Tree_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3623.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Black_Pepper_Flower_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3622.jpg/500px-Black_Pepper_Flower_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3622.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Black_Pepper_Flower_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3622.jpg/1280px-Black_Pepper_Flower_-_Kerala_-_IMG_3622.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumb